D5 complete: verify_and_record proof-of-work verification for a pull request.

Added a `verify_and_record` agent tool that attaches real evidence to a PR before
its author claims it is done. The tool derives a test plan from the PR's own diff,
runs the user flows with Playwright against a local static app (a recorded video and
a screenshot per flow), saves the artifacts, and appends a `## Verification`
checklist with the artifact links to the PR body through the D1 `PrProvider`.

## What was produced
- `src/agent/prVerification.ts` (638 lines): the plan derivation, the Playwright
  runner, the checklist renderer and the idempotent section appender. Pure
  functions (`planFromDiff`, `renderVerificationChecklist`, `appendVerificationSection`,
  `artifactLink`, `slug`, `fixtureFlows`) plus one async runner (`runPrVerification`).
- `src/tools/verifyAndRecordTools.ts` (233 lines): the tool schema and `run()`. Reads
  `git diff <base>...HEAD` from the workspace, resolves the provider through the D2
  `resolvePrProvider` seam (no network in tests) and writes the body through the new
  `setPrBody` method.
- `src/tools/gitPrProvider.ts`: added `setPrBody(repo, number, body)` to the
  `PrProvider` interface and both implementations - `GitHubPrProvider` issues
  `PATCH /repos/{repo}/pulls/{number}`; `LocalPrProvider` stores the new body so the
  section persists in tests.
- `src/modes/catalog.ts`: `verify_and_record` added to the `GIT` tool set, so it is
  available in the git/PR modes (and the modes that extend them).
- `src/setup/runtime.ts`: the tool registered alongside `createCiWatchTool`.
- `prompts/loam-master.md` + `src/agent/masterPromptText.ts` (regenerated via
  `npm run gen:master-prompt`): a §6.3 tool-catalog row and a §8.5 rule, matching the
  D2 `ci_watch` wiring pattern. The `coding-prompt.snap.json` snapshot
  `masterPromptSha256` was updated (`499c8c39...` -> `35b2bf36...`).

## Acceptance criteria
- **Plan derived from the diff, not invented.** `planFromDiff` parses a unified diff,
  finds changed paths, anchors interaction flows in selectors the diff itself
  introduces (`selectorFromDiffText`), and never claims a flow the diff does not
  support (`isClaimedByDiff`). A declarative fixture plan (`PrVerificationFixture`) is
  supported for cases where the diff does not name the page.
- **Real Playwright evidence, per flow.** `runPrVerification` serves the app over a
  loopback-only static server and runs each flow in its own browser context, recording
  a video and a screenshot into the task artifacts directory (slugged file names).
- **Fail-closed.** A missing PR number, an empty local app root, or an app root that
  escapes the workspace is refused before anything runs; an empty plan is refused
  rather than running nothing. A failing flow reports `Verification failed` and does
  not claim success.
- **Idempotent PR body update.** `appendVerificationSection` is guarded by a marker
  comment, so re-running replaces the previous `## Verification` section instead of
  appending a second one, and preserves the original body.
- **`noPost` for local-only runs.** With `noPost` the plan still runs but the PR body
  is not written.
- **Artifacts always linked or named missing.** A captured artifact is linked; a
  missing one is reported as missing rather than silently dropped.

## Files
- `src/agent/prVerification.ts` - new, plan derivation + runner + renderer.
- `src/tools/verifyAndRecordTools.ts` - new, tool schema + `run()` + `prDiff`.
- `src/agent/__tests__/prVerification.test.ts` - new, 12 tests.
- `src/tools/__tests__/verifyAndRecord.test.ts` - new, 7 tests (real git repo,
  `LocalPrProvider`, real Playwright, mocked GitHub fetch).
- `src/tools/__tests__/ciWatch.test.ts` - 3 `setPrBody` stubs added to the existing
  fake providers (interface contract only; no assertion weakened).
- `src/tools/gitPrProvider.ts` - `setPrBody` on the interface + both implementations.
- `src/modes/catalog.ts`, `src/setup/runtime.ts` - registration/allowlisting.
- `prompts/loam-master.md`, `src/agent/masterPromptText.ts`,
  `src/agent/__tests__/__snapshots__/coding-prompt.snap.json` - prompt wiring.

## Defects found and fixed while implementing
**1. The tool test repo defaulted to `master`, not `main`.** `seedRepo()` used a plain
`git init`, which on this machine creates `master`, while the tool's default diff base
is `main`, so the first version of the test had no diff to derive a plan from. The
seeding now runs `git init -q -b main` and the tests pass.

**2. The D5 prompt wiring was missing.** The previous handoff recorded that
`masterPromptText.ts` and `prompts/loam-master.md` had been edited, but both were
byte-identical to HEAD and `verify_and_record` was absent from both. The §6.3 row and
the §8.5 rule were added (following the D2 `ci_watch` pattern), the master prompt
asset was regenerated, and the snapshot hash updated.

