Independent end-to-end probe (no stubs, real production objects)
---------------------------------------------------------------
A standalone probe composed the real registry, tool, event and protocol mapper:
  registry -> tool.run -> emitted AgentEvent -> mapAgentEvent -> ChatEvent[]
written outside the worktree (%TEMP%\d17-e2e-probe.mts, run with
`node --import tsx`), 15/15 checks passed:
  - always-on: present in ALWAYS_ON_TOOLS; granted when registered+not denied;
    withheld when denied; never granted when unregistered; reachable through
    `registry.forAllowlist(merged)`.
  - happy path: tool.run returns ok + guidance, emits exactly one
    `environment_issue` AgentEvent carrying both `message` and `details`.
  - mapping: that event maps to exactly one `environmentIssue` ChatEvent with
    the same message/details plus a non-empty id and numeric timestamp.
  - optional field: omitting `details` leaves the key absent on BOTH the agent
    event and the mapped chat event (not synthesized).
  - validation: blank, over-long (2001 chars) and missing `message` are all
    rejected with ok:false and emit nothing.
